        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Seoul</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">18 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Baekje founded its capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wiryeseong">Wiryeseong</a>, in 18 BCE, believed to lie within the bounds of present-day Seoul; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taejo-of-joseon">Yi Seong-gye</a>, founder of the Joseon dynasty, chose Hanyang as his new capital in September 1394, and construction began in October 1394.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On both banks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-river">Han River</a> in the north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, in a mountainous and hilly landscape with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhansan">Bukhansan</a> on its northern edge.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wiryeseong">Wiryeseong</a>, the capital of Baekje; the Joseon capital of Hanyang and Hanseong; the Fortress Wall and its gates; the Five Grand Palaces; Japanese rule as Keijo; the four battles for the city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korean-war">Korean War</a>; the rebuilding of the city and the growth of Gangnam</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Seoul is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, with about 9.6 million residents, and the only special metropolitan city in the country.</span></div>
